  ('07b6b778-8c62-473f-a973-949ff77016b5'::uuid, '330 meters tall. Built in 1889. Made of iron. Lattice tower construction. Designed by Gustave Eiffel and team. Engineered by Maurice Koechlin. Engineered by Émile Nouguier. Architectural design by Stephen Sauvestre. Pyramidal shape. Used as an observation tower. Functions as a communication tower. Hosts FM radio transmitters. Broadcasts DVB-T digital television signals. Historic monument from the modern period. Inscribed as a protected heritage site in 1964. Receives around 7 million visitors annually. Painted in a brownish-grey colour (#706550). One of the most iconic lattice iron structures in the world. Initially criticized by many artists and intellectuals upon construction. Originally granted a 20-year permit before becoming permanent due to its utility for communication', '[0.074811056,0.20445418,-0.029525,0.01442498,-0.042826794,0.012018196,-0.0016662544,0.09245563,-0.028462533,-0.032585625,-0.15021595,0.09468803,0.156471,0.042579122,-0.14241877,-0.07636903,0.15164982,-0.11287649,-0.013586876,0.012224469,0.026611742,-0.12286361,0.04027033,-0.10878065,0.06884033,0.06715196,-0.06009126,0.16724457,0.18649074,0.05686513,-0.033870287,0.011894716,0.07477364,0.14651687,-0.053295664,0.09442457,0.07908832,-0.09397182,-0.1259225,-0.084662944,-0.074961714,0.028426632,0.11973701,-0.007812145,-0.056566015,0.010352172,0.1370027,-0.05078316,-0.09684942,-0.08717699,0.066651575,0.11441826,0.14152151,-0.095520124,0.0468406,-0.08629925,0.0061021056,-0.11705502,-0.016296064,0.006391596,0.18350276,0.012320338,-0.06841286,-0.08603559,0.0820477,0.041929886,-0.06030833,-0.023525547,0.18945614,-0.014026577,0.16126457,0.059035473,0.043532573,0.08619581,0.14016204,-0.073539265,-0.06683109,-0.0051795905,-0.07452836,-0.07517881,-0.038607813,-0.036356352,-0.0075137476,0.100908205,0.032123603,0.043388978,-0.21159431,0.17430507,-0.06598519,-0.0979804,0.1406474,0.099256516,-0.10460829,0.13265921,-0.04914116,-0.017735697,-0.10526564,0.00731797