  ('937cac4c-abc3-443f-9e3b-d26ba1ca587c'::uuid, 'Has a height of 96 meters. Roof height is 35 meters. Has a pyramidal roof shape. Is a tower. Contains the largest bell, known for its deep chime. Completed in 1859 after construction began in the 1840s. Designed by architect Augustus Pugin in Gothic Revival style. Located within a historic parliamentary estate along the River Thames. Features four large clock faces, each over 7 meters in diameter. Houses a clock mechanism weighing approximately 5 tons. Main bell weighs about 13.7 tons and strikes every hour. _200 steps to reach the belfry via spiral staircase. _Each clock face has a perimeter of about 118 feet (36 meters). _A defining feature of the city''s skyline since the Victorian era. _Exemplifies Gothic Revival architecture with ornate stonework and spires. _Underwent major restoration from 2017 to 2022, including structural repairs and repainting', '[0.18966056,-0.0059078606,0.16200855,-0.058867816,-0.21823984,0.025683617,-0.1511539,-0.018817855,-0.27241212,-0.029234823,-0.14577289,0.008351498,0.024958272,-0.10274286,-0.08793587,0.03232536,0.09888997,-0.1069069,-0.03253911,0.028578272,0.038920753,-0.09422441,0.122891985,0.15101524,0.026106894,0.0620858,-0.12451811,0.08839648,0.015974285,-0.14076833,-0.028543204,0.07321734,0.050761677,-0.033071227,0.033649437,0.025010245,0.20208967,0.03988697,0.026170135,-0.121028215,0.028615212,0.013013469,0.096630566,0.10278532,-0.01459569,0.17466405,-0.018444281,-0.045145214,-0.18898338,-0.11565583,0.15068324,0.15030015,0.06246816,-0.046669044,-0.046480596,0.1854989,-0.103067,-0.057981152,0.10637907,0.030438801,0.028554048,0.18913075,-0.26021972,0.018103082,-0.019119607,0.017993562,-0.23114303,-0.08203484,0.061235033,-0.08656928,0.15780462,-0.152083,-0.046046574,0.039030768,0.01572745,-0.19119287,0.10142101,-0.12681635,-0.09426673,-0.036634684,-0.09780125,-0.0068755546,-0.0022834418,0.15872772,0.1341312,-0.012158215,-0.035069957,0.113325395,-0.15976399,0.0011435049,0.1473714