  ('d91d9ab0-1587-4505-9489-1355984ae87a'::uuid, 'Has a white roof. Construction started in 1632. Is a mausoleum. UNESCO World Heritage site. Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1983. Recognized by UNESCO for representing a masterpiece of human creativity. Built as a tomb for an empress who died during childbirth. Commissioned by the Mughal emperor Shah Jahan. Took more than 20 years to complete construction. Main structure is built from white marble. White marble was sourced from Makrana, Rajasthan. Has four minarets flanking the main dome. Stands 73 meters tall including the finial and platform. Involved over 17,000 artisans and laborers during construction. ''Pietra dura'' inlay work uses 28 types of precious and semi-precious stones. ''Mirrored perfectly in the Yamuna River when viewed from the gardens''. ''Surrounded by a formal Mughal garden divided into four quadrants''. ''Features a large central dome with an interior height of over 58 meters''. ''Quranic verses are inscribed in black marble using elegant calligraphy''', '[0.089736074,0.33504245,-0.10424253,-0.016496805,-0.2350452,-0.16134685,-0.12715468,-0.035166334,-0.035487648,-0.0761392,-0.150175,-0.19154206,0.14890833,0.052323963,0.08995901,-0.056320008,0.17451338,0.039975934,-0.0008991994,-0.13185492,0.031717114,-0.119255506,0.1951099,-0.031140665,-0.030879071,0.13658845,-0.1388233,0.018265603,0.1255696,-0.12149544,-0.08813226,0.055906788,-0.022829002,-0.045139425,0.05788555,0.06262577,0.06023127,0.036724024,0.08961246,-0.116142176,0.09435187,0.046567217,0.004343385,0.047348987,0.034319267,0.045117315,-0.09915546,-0.10523384,0.014604248,-0.13836923,-0.051099308,-0.014874052,-0.026529316,0.025830396,0.034938548,-0.19327253,-0.08024895,-0.01478678,0.120600924,-0.044853352,-0.06697881,0.16909927,-0.0018911464,-0.020675896,0.102519,-0.1823011,-0.043818004,-0.066301964,0.06449759,-0.16209821,0.15163127,-0.054230522,0.061349098,-0.053764295,-0.19670674,-0.08768442,0.06353271,0.10034498,-0.34455246,-