  ('760cc1f6-892e-4165-8e7a-28f530e63695'::uuid, 'Rises 348 meters above the surrounding desert. Has a circumference of approximately 9.4 kilometers. Formed from arkose sandstone with high feldspar content. Geological formation began over 500 million years ago. Exposed due to tectonic uplift during the Cenozoic era. Sacred site for the Anangu Aboriginal people. Owned and jointly managed by the Anangu traditional custodians. Managed jointly by traditional owners and Parks Australia. Listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site for both natural and cultural values. One of few sites with dual UNESCO recognition for natural and cultural significance. Climbing has been prohibited since October 2019 out of respect for traditional owners. Surface color shifts dramatically with sunlight, time of day, and weather. Situated within a protected national park in central Australia. Receives less than 300 millimeters of rain per year on average. Geologically linked to the ancient Petermann Orogeny and Great Artesian Basin system', '[0.06985864,0.21336564,0.041141097,-0.039766032,0.04885183,-0.016205192,-0.080020055,-0.023396555,-0.10710985,0.20471323,-0.09041381,-0.3952941,-0.030892884,0.20424247,0.05086825,0.077933095,-0.13320783,-0.05399586,0.0694281,0.051538873,0.015827674,0.019965885,0.023600984,0.0030182148,-0.04435408,-0.045443337,-0.10470469,0.13772981,0.13616903,-0.059668645,-0.06348627,0.087374315,0.06602664,-0.10012077,0.14936829,0.06097967,-0.06291348,-0.15479793,-0.061714288,-0.12843575,0.043112792,0.07738322,0.10246172,-0.18010032,-0.058918554,0.05655327,0.09706755,0.038111754,-0.01031572,0.12235485,0.14735338,0.123185016,-0.009166007,-0.07662388,-0.065546714,-0.08630021,0.0087142475,-0.28694153,-0.014954485,-0.082329735,0.20735861,0.08083451,-0.21535978,-0.02101564,-0.00397274,-0.046119392,-0.22585647,-0.04890449,0.1009402,-0.08748932,0.018053498,-0.05952923,0.09548406,-0.09226918,0.009371152,0.07878402,0.06931985,0.12585747,-0.17891859,-0.17600143,0.06001512,0.18271194,0.