  ('67c2010f-11c3-42f7-b0e1-a5aab9301582'::uuid, 'Man-made monument. Recognized as a global landmark. Located in Brazil. Classified as a tourist attraction. Completed in 1931. Designed by French sculptor Paul Landowski. Structural engineering by Heitor da Silva Costa. Made of reinforced concrete and soapstone tiles. The statue stands 30 meters tall. Sits on an 8-meter-tall pedestal. Total height including pedestal is 38 meters. Weighs approximately 220 tons. Named one of the New Seven Wonders of the World in 2007. Accessible via a 2.5 km mountain railway from base to summit. Located at an elevation of 645 meters above sea level. Has an arm span of 28 meters from fingertip to fingertip. Struck by lightning multiple times annually due to exposed location. Underwent major restorations in 2010 and 2015 for structural and surface repairs', '[0.028387617,0.14770184,0.05228557,0.014390545,-0.05498564,-0.052908905,-0.02973704,0.15887411,-0.036229916,0.03517555,-0.054959595,-0.075819425,-0.039656896,0.107111946,-0.13588348,-0.033101544,0.02107558,0.035050407,0.022313956,0.053866114,0.22898369,-0.045083854,0.0068273908,0.06334622,0.031876758,0.06826675,-0.10161981,0.066393234,0.070409186,-0.063954964,-0.048728205,0.005242903,-0.020678606,-0.011624182,-0.035568375,0.110890836,0.08303779,0.034244478,0.055962615,-0.086409494,-0.07387315,-0.09601171,0.11407977,0.0843659,0.08006444,0.11794428,0.07292607,-0.017080395,-0.0030060415,-0.09021811,0.020451631,0.0475023,0.032118164,-0.08704707,-0.021299839,-0.006003855,0.038207468,-0.1549866,0.10396228,0.054420613,0.19559644,0.04816412,0.053673517,0.020921413,-0.016540773,-0.08698013,-0.1315794,-0.060380004,-0.011308497,0.13752402,0.26033023,-0.10319412,0.09693572,-0.092764646,0.06843803,-0.03870951,-0.032638993,0.047291465,-0.10149648,-0.017935773,0.1177132,0.015513025,0.06889826,0.088512495,-0.013993749,0.008417738,0.016642235,0.050274003,-0.09870587,-0.018098995,0.118147075,0.013163716,-0.13858928,0.06368916,-0.04859866,0.02758933,-0.