  ('4a549d49-0879-47a8-b00c-12782e1b1a2f'::uuid, 'Is a pyramid-shaped structure. Stands 138.8 meters tall. Has approximately 40 structural levels. Constructed in the 26th century BCE. Is the oldest of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World. Is the only one of the Seven Wonders still largely intact. Built as a tomb for Pharaoh Khufu (Cheops). Features ancient Egyptian architectural style. Constructed using limestone, Tora-limestone, and granite. Has a pyramidal roof shape. Roof has an orange-yellow hue (#F69B3C). Officially designated as a historic tomb. Allows public access with an entry fee of around $5.70. Originates from the ancient Egyptian civilization. Ranked among top-tier global landmarks (level 2). Listed on English Wikipedia as a notable site. Also documented on German Wikipedia under Cheops-Pyramide. Has street-level imagery available via Mapillary platform. Includes brick in roof or upper core layers, possibly from later modifications or internal structure', '[0.041722484,0.18193963,-0.021305077,-0.021772094,-0.18180603,-0.1224374,-0.10485705,0.15084568,-0.07067954,-0.011937404,-0.14778967,-0.15488967,0.04192444,-0.05611133,-0.02082416,-0.07538633,0.029836489,0.00082906894,0.016224295,-0.09824996,0.06445377,-0.17506486,0.20113884,0.02187812,0.04092788,0.020033643,-0.10192253,0.1151609,0.10511281,-0.12831548,0.052384544,-0.055335812,-0.010522766,0.019339636,0.06350699,0.15272325,0.060985286,-0.080222845,-0.030569848,-0.0023123757,0.06299936,0.08599551,0.021844547,-0.037710305,0.108752176,0.16818798,0.08502726,-0.23070577,-0.13923883,-0.05917099,-0.025626441,-0.078514546,-0.024198703,0.029683061,-0.027098447,-0.023434106,0.0015670229,-0.15655482,0.053670973,-0.029375743,0.1331594,-0.015757285,-0.017724525,-0.114145234,-0.02996294,0.066020295,-0.100034036,-0.09767963,0.14622936,-0.1426267,0.018797029,-0.061669957,0.13358721,0.13395733,0.0137427915,-0.20563908,0.081672944,-0.10603227,-0.16081984,-0.108652756,0.06450254,0.10704331,0.031536113,0.086209,-0.1206